 "build": {
  "id": "50ee019c-17b8-4d8b-b318-d46eaa5ef154",
  "title": "Eternal Furry Dungeon(leveling) Tank",
  "description": "[overview]\nCongratz, you are now a Furry on their period with anger issues :)\nThis build is primarily for people who like to spam dungeons while leveling\n\nThis is a WIP! \nI am open for discussions, testing and theory-crafting stuff.\n\n## Warning\nThis class scales with Player Skill.\nIf you are confident with kiting, spacing, preemptive CD usage and on-the-spot adaptation you will excel!\nIf you pull pack-by-pack, you will be fine. \nIf you try to chain-pull without using the classes abilities and strengths you will be A) cosplaying as a furry floor-mat or B) your healers HPS will mean Heart-attacks per Second...\n\nPost feedback/ideas/tips/secrets and i will work them into the guide.\n\n**GL & HF!**\n\n[talents]\nWe are pretty locked in for the majority of the Talent Tree. \nThe Major debate is the choice for the last 2 Points.\n\n### Eternal Tree\nMentioning talents not picked: \n**Appetite for Blood**: BIG DPS boost for your primary spam button. maybe worth dropping **Rejuvenating Shadows** for this.\n**Packleader**: **Currently bait, don't**. Check if bat's remain after they hit once, if they stick around -> *this may be worth.*\n**Festering Maw**: Can be good, but i would not bother with it since we are already very mobile.\n**Infection**: Too slow for us. If we take a swing-timer of 3,3s this would take 33s to fully stack, and it has a 6 SECOND DURATION. It will fall off on any transition, any movement. You auto attack another enemy -> falls off. You miss one auto attack -> falls off. You don't have a bleed up -> falls off.....  If you pick **Infection** your swing timer *needs to be below 2.85s* or you grief yourself!\n**Blood Moon**/**Shadows in the Night**: it's *meh* at best. 3% heal of all damage is solid enough to justify picking it up, but the conditions cuck you too much. If they reverse conditions it may be worth.\nPick any **Call of the Darkwing** talents last, as their value comes from the finisher **Shadow Strength**.\n\nFor the finishers:\n**Bloody Claws**: This talent is really good, for a \"Blood Pact Chaining\" Main Tank build, this is not a MT build :)\n**Eyes In The Night**: As of right now, this is one of the weakest finishers i have seen. 1 **Call of the Darkwing** per 5 sec is just bad. And that is assuming full proc rate. \nThe threat is not worth mentioning, since who procs it is mostly *random melees doing melee stuff*, and at **best** it's a taunt on a 5s CD.\n\n### Class Tree\nChange **Blood Trails** to **Everhungry** if you want a more DPS(ego) play-style.\nWith that logic you can change **Blood Bond** to **Nightmare**, **Nightmare** has some funny stuff going on, but it's mostly a DPS boost.\nAs for **Transfusion**, it's a good spell, but the alternatives are just better.\nAnd **Predator** is never up for discussion, 1% Crit damage is not worth.\n\nOn the \"Why do you pick **Liquify** and **Bloodmoon Power** over XYZ?\" question:\n1) You can make a macro to cancelaura **Curse Form** and cast **Liquify**, thus we bypass the \"requires mortal form\".\n2) You can use it to buffer void zones or survive big \"near boss\" blasts or certain **One Shot** abilities/mechanics.\n3) The other Talents are *useless* or *bait*. The other options, if you don't wish to bother with **Liquify**, are **Easy Prey** and **Life Scent**.\nTIP: Make your macro reusable, e.g. Cancel aura **Curse Form** -> Cast **Liquify** -> Cancle aura **Liquify** -> Cast **Curse Form**\nIf you belong in the \"hit button 50 times\" category, make 2 macro's. One to swap into **Liquify**, one to swap into **Curse Form**...\nYou do not want to get stuck in **Liquify** because the boss will be upset and *decided he is gonna play with the melees if he can't diddle you*! You essentially Blessing Of Protection yourself, you can work in the AOE Taunt into the macro if you want to.\n(I will post macro's in a bit, still WIP segment)\n\n\nFor me **Blood Bond** is a must though, and the target is simple -> **HEALER**\nThere are plenty of **caster mobs** that stay stuck in nirvana and your healer is the only one stacking aggro on them, they CAN and WILL kill your healer, **Blood Bond prevents that**. \nYou can put **Blood Bond** on someone else, depending on either your dungeon knowledge or if you have a DPS buddy to coordinate with. Overall **Blood Moon** is a solid to VERY STRONG talent.\nI do prefer to put it on the Healer for the simple reason that it gives Bro-Points, and that's always helpful.\n\n[rotation]\nThis Spec has more of a priority-list then a true rotation.\n\n### Group pulls\n1) Keep up **Rot Claw**, never let it sit on 2 stacks.\n2) Use **Claw Sweep** when you have Rage\n3) Use Rage generators, either the CD(HP -> 50 Rage converter) one, or the single target basic one.\n\n###Single Target\n1) Keep up **Hypovolemic Shock** (AP debuff), **Rotclaw**, **Bloodfang Bite**\n2) Spam **Bloodfang Bite**\n3) Spam rage generator\n\nAs for **How To** dungeon pull:\n1) Tell your DPS's to watch their single target threat during *grouping pulls*!\n2) Use **Rotclaw** on the first and second pack you pull to lock them onto you. (DPS's will focus on these mobs most).\n3) Use **Claw Sweep**, or **Rotclaw** if available, when collecting packs along the way.\n4) **Taunt** and **Hypovolimic shock** to bring in stragglers.\n5) Once you have enough mobs start kiting in a Circle to group up the mobs, use your **AOE** while staying out of melee range.\n6) When the Mobs are starting to group up use your 30% increased HP CDs **before** going in!\n7) Use **Blood Pact** to face tank\n8) If it looks dicey -> **start kiting again**\nHow big you pull mostly depends on A) your skill and B) how based your healer is ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯\n\n[stats]\n**Core Stats**: Agility -> Armor -> Stamina -> Def Stats\n**\"Nice\" Stats**: Strength -> Crit -> AP\n\n[gear]\nLeatherworking crafted gear is absolutely OP, but it requires time. \nIf you wanna invest the time however it is **awesome**.\n\n[leveling]\nQueueueueu Dungeons. If you find a Based Healer, add them to Friends-list and spam Dungeons with them.\n\n[tips]\nCaster mobs can(will) be your downfall, downsize your pulls.",
